value.text:
Confirmed upstream SDK recovery regression in 2026.10.23. The Node 26 CI test SIGKILL during root write leaves the previous budget and transcript intact fails with lock_conflict, reason lock_owner_dead, after roughly 3040 ms. Node 22 reaches only the separate changelog drift. A deterministic minimal SDK repro confirms that the commit fence leaves a cleanup gate that outlives the default 3000 ms wait; dead-owner takeover succeeds once the gate expires. The 2026.10.23 changelog documents new fencing (GH-1549), but does not document removal or delay of dead-owner recovery. Do not hide this behind package retries, longer test waits, skipped tests, or lowered coverage.

Minimal reproduction, run as a module in a package with SDK 2026.10.23 installed:
```js
import { mkdtempSync, writeFileSync, rmSync } from 'node:fs';
import { tmpdir } from 'node:os';
import { fork } from 'node:child_process';
import { join } from 'node:path';
import { pathToFileURL } from 'node:url';
import { createRequire } from 'node:module';
const require = createRequire(join(process.cwd(), 'package.json'));
const sdkUrl = pathToFileURL(require.resolve('@unbrained/pm-cli/sdk')).href;
const { acquireLockLease, isPmCliExpectedError } = await import(sdkUrl);
const root = mkdtempSync(join(tmpdir(), 'pm-fence-repro-'));
const childPath = join(root, 'writer.mjs');
writeFileSync(childPath, `
const { acquireLockLease } = await import(${JSON.stringify(sdkUrl)});
const lease = await acquireLockLease(${JSON.stringify(root)}, 'repro-item', 1, 'writer', false, false, 0);
await lease.fence(async () => {
  setInterval(() => {}, 1000);
  process.send('fenced');
  await new Promise(() => {});
});
`);
const child = fork(childPath, {stdio:['ignore','ignore','inherit','ipc']});
try {
  await new Promise((resolve,reject) => { child.once('message',resolve); child.once('error',reject); child.once('exit',code=>reject(new Error('writer exited '+code))); });
  const exited = new Promise(resolve => child.once('exit',resolve));
  child.kill('SIGKILL');
  await exited;
  await new Promise(resolve => setTimeout(resolve, 1200));
  let started = Date.now();
  try {
    const lease = await acquireLockLease(root, 'repro-item', 1, 'reader', false, false, 3000);
    await lease.release();
    console.log('early takeover succeeded',Date.now()-started);
  } catch(error) {
    console.log(JSON.stringify({code:error.code,reason:isPmCliExpectedError(error)?error.context.reason:undefined,elapsed_ms:Date.now()-started}));
  }
  await new Promise(resolve => setTimeout(resolve,10500));
  started=Date.now();
  const lease = await acquireLockLease(root, 'repro-item', 1, 'reader', false, false, 3000);
  await lease.release();
  console.log('takeover after gate expiry succeeded',Date.now()-started);
} finally { child.kill('SIGKILL'); rmSync(root,{recursive:true,force:true}); }
```
Observed: {"code":"lock_conflict","reason":"lock_owner_dead","elapsed_ms":3029}; the identical acquisition succeeds after gate expiry. The reproduction sends its readiness message from inside lease.fence and keeps the child alive until SIGKILL. It uses only a synthetic tracker and removes its own scratch directory. Existing production code is preserved; the uncommitted retry wrapper and tests are retained outside the package for review only.
